WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:23.560
So as many of you know, Congresswoman Alexandria
[inaudible] Cortez has endorsed Bernie Sanders

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:28.310
for president. Now, I've already said, and
some of you disagree with me, I don't believe

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:35.720
that AOC endorsement is going to do that much
for Bernie because her constituency is more

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.360
than likely already supporting Bernie. What
I mean by that is if you are someone who is

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:46.750
of the mindset that I don't know who I'm going
to support, but once AOC says who she's supporting,

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.950
I'm going to support someone.

00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:53.040
It's not that likely that that's the position
you're in. You're probably already leaning

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:56.930
towards, we're supporting Bernie Sanders.
So I know some of you disagree with that assessment.

00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:01.340
That's fine. It's a difference of opinion.
Two beautiful thing. Okay? Something interesting

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:07.580
happened when Bernie Sanders and AOC were
interviewed on the day of their massive rally.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:12.280
I believe that this was the biggest rally
for any candidate in the 2020 election cycle.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:17.260
Just a massive, massive rally at which a AOC
endorsed Bernie. Uh, I dunno if this was right

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:23.870
before or after the event, but a reporter
went to AOC and sort of played the identity

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:31.480
politics games saying why are you a woman
of color endorsing an old white guy like Bernie

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.730
Sanders who was sitting right next to AOC
during this interview? And there are many

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:39.260
things that I want to comment on here, but
first let's look at the video.

00:01:39.260 --> 00:01:44.640
You made history with your election and you
both are part of the most diverse Congress

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:51.080
in history. This is also the most diverse
democratic presidential field ever. I'm going

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:55.470
to be a little blunt with you Congresswoman
and don't take offense Senator, but as a woman

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:59.520
of color, why back in old white guy and is
this the future of the party? Yeah, you know,

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.540
I think I'm actually very excited about

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:10.979
this partnership because it shows what we
have to do in our country is that we have

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:15.800
to come together across race, across gender,
across generation and across, across class

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:19.600
in order to establish our basic systems as
rights.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:24.590
So AOC, his answer is, is basically fine,
but we really need to talk more broadly about

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:28.290
this question because there's some important
stuff here. Now, some people wrote to me when

00:02:28.290 --> 00:02:32.689
they saw this video, this question and said,
David, look at this at some kind of disgusting

00:02:32.689 --> 00:02:39.239
reverse identity politics thing and it's terrible.
Others wrote to me and said, you know, AOC

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:44.409
has talked about the importance of supporting
minority politicians so she could have supported

00:02:44.409 --> 00:02:49.810
or endorsed Camilla Harris. She could have
endorsed Corey Booker or Tulsa Gabard or Andrew

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:56.730
Yang, but she is instead endorsing Bernie,
the old white guy. And it's a good thing to

00:02:56.730 --> 00:03:02.200
bring this up to her and to give her an opportunity
to explain why she decided to endorse the

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:06.469
old white guy. Now the reality is that there's
multiple analyses here and I think we should

00:03:06.469 --> 00:03:09.459
make all of them in order to really do this
properly.

00:03:09.459 --> 00:03:14.799
In principle, there is nothing wrong with
a reporter saying, listen, Congresswoman,

00:03:14.799 --> 00:03:19.750
you've saidX is important. How does your endorsement
of Bernie square with that? And in this case

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:24.249
it's, you've said supporting minority politicians
is important. How does endorsing Bernie square

00:03:24.249 --> 00:03:30.540
with that no problem. And of course the answer
is, well Bernie's platform and Bernie's policies

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.969
would get directly to the heart of many of
the inequalities that I want to solve. And

00:03:34.969 --> 00:03:40.489
a lot of those inequalities run across racial
lines. So Bernie's identity is not an issue

00:03:40.489 --> 00:03:48.569
here. His platform is at issue and by supporting
Bernie I N supporting minority Americans of

00:03:48.569 --> 00:03:54.400
all stripes, that would be a completely reasonable
thing to do. What I think people are reacting

00:03:54.400 --> 00:04:01.739
to is that the reporter seems to be doing
it to sort of be edgy and controversial or

00:04:01.739 --> 00:04:06.900
whatever. Calling Bernie an old white guy
to his face as part of the optics of the whole

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:07.900
thing.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:11.189
And I get it that it feels sort of deliberately
sensationalist and some people aren't liking

00:04:11.189 --> 00:04:15.919
that. So I understand that. But there's another
issue here that I have not heard discussed

00:04:15.919 --> 00:04:22.580
anywhere, which is that Bernie Sanders is
part of a minority group that is one of the

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:29.750
most persecuted minority groups in human history.
Bernie Sanders is Jewish and this is not politically

00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:34.870
correct, but you know, I don't care about
that. There are stereotypes and conspiracies

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:41.830
about Jews and money and power in the United
States and unfortunately it has become almost

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:47.510
like a fo paw on the left to talk about Jews
as a minority group that has suffered massive

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:52.420
historical discrimination. Genocide attempted
against, Jews kicked out of, I don't even

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:56.540
know how many countries it is. So there's
another angle to this that is an important

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:02.480
one to discuss if you want to play the game
that the is playing, which is aside from what's

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:09.380
important being the platform of Bernie, not
Bernie's identity, Bernie's identity and Bernie's

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:12.720
story are of minority struggle.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:17.880
Bernie's parents came to the United States
before the Holocaust. They did the, you know,

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:23.210
outsider immigrant struggle thing for lack
of a better term, but not everybody in Bernie's

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:28.160
family made it to the United States. Relatives
of Bernie's were killed in German, occupied

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:33.870
Poland during the Holocaust and Bernie Sanders,
like many Jewish Americans, was front and

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:40.180
center as a participant in the civil rights
movement of the second half of the 20th century.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:45.690
So you can analyze this by saying the question
was a bad one, a at minimum it was a poorly

00:05:45.690 --> 00:05:51.480
asked question. You can say, well, AOC is
endorsement is the correct one because she's

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:57.130
focusing on platform over identity, but even
if you don't want to do any of that stuff

00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:03.740
and you want to do an identity politics analysis,
it shouldn't be a foe paw for Bernie's identity

00:06:03.740 --> 00:06:09.780
and Bernie's family history to be part of
the story as it is for so many Jews who became

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:15.090
key players and partners in the fight for
civil rights of all kinds, for all sorts of

00:06:15.090 --> 00:06:17.930
people in the United States and around the
world.

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:22.190
Let me know what you think about this. Let
me know what your reaction is to the video.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:27.390
Let me know what you think about [inaudible]
answer and handling of it, but also let me

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:33.230
know what you think about the other analysis
that exists. If we want to suspend, at least

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:40.650
for me, if, if I suspend for a moment, my
disdain for these types of identity politics,

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:46.220
alliances, allegiances, analyses, call them
what they want. There's actually an interesting

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:53.110
identity story that links Bernie Sanders to
a struggle for racial equality struggle for

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:58.310
a class equality. And that's not a story that's
being told. And I think it's a story that

00:06:58.310 --> 00:07:03.440
is considered, as I said, a [inaudible], a
unfortunately among many on the left and also

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:07.060
among the white nationalists, right. And by
the way, who see Jews as you know, the Uber

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:11.260
privileged of any, uh, of any group. Uh, as
we've heard many times, even from people I've

00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:14.771
interviewed on the program, I want to hear
from you. Leave me a reply on YouTube. If

00:07:14.771 --> 00:07:15.771
you're watching [inaudible]

00:07:15.771 --> 00:07:21.590
it's on YouTube or send me a tweet at [inaudible]
Pacman. How do you interpret all of this?

00:07:21.590 --> 00:07:21.800
Quick break right back after this

